    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Reliable indicators of neighborhood stability and community cohesion can be obtained from various data sources, including:\n\n1. Socio-economic indicators: Median household income, poverty rates, and educational attainment of the population.\n2. Demographic data: Age structure, household size, marital rates, and immigrant density.\n3. Crime statistics: Incidence rates of violent and property crimes.\n4. Economic activity metrics: Foot traffic, businesses per capita, and local employment rates.\n5. Infrastructure and services: Availability of public transportation, healthcare facilities, and public services (e.g., schools, libraries).\n6. Online reviews and ratings: To gauge community engagement and overall neighborhood reputation.\n7. Census data: Tracts or zip codes can be used to estimate local demographics and socioeconomic trends.\n\nSome specific features that may correlate with lower default rates include:\n\n1. Higher median household income.\n2. Lower poverty rates.\n3. Higher educational attainment rates.\n4. Lower crime rates.\n5. Increased foot traffic and local employment opportunities.\n6. Stable or improving infrastructure and services.",
